\section{Analyzing Search Calling Decisions}
\label{sec:webtoolcall}

%The first stage of the Web-search lifecycle is deciding whether external knowledge is necessary or whether the model's parametric knowledge is sufficient.
%
Web search is invoked when LLM agents {\it decide} that they need additional (external) knowledge, i.e., their parametric (internal) knowledge is insufficient, to respond to a user prompt. 
%
So we begin by analyzing agents' decisions to search the Web. 
%
