\subsection{Need for Search Calling}

The observed differences in Web-search behavior naturally raise the question: \textit{\textbf{Does frequent Web search invocations improve response quality?}} To answer this question, in Table \ref{tab:replay}, we compare responses under three settings in the \invitro\ setup: (i) prompts for which the model autonomously invoked Web search (\textit{Web-calling samples}), (ii) the same prompts with Web search disabled (\textit{Web-calling samples in No Web mode}), and (iii) prompts for which the model chose not to invoke Web search (\textit{No Web-calling samples}). 
Response quality is evaluated using three complementary metrics: factuality, completeness, and relevance, measuring the correctness, coverage, and how well the response addresses the user's request, respectively. Appendix~\ref{app:replays_eval_criteria} describes the evaluation protocol.
