\if 0
\textbf{\textit{What querying strategies emerge in the \invivo\ traces?}} Figures~\ref{fig:total_Web_queries_rev}  and \ref{fig:iterations_per_prompt_rev} characterize the number of Web queries and iterations associated with each user prompt, while the distributions of fan-out queries and iterations are provided in Appendix Figure~\ref{fig:number_of_query_reformulations_and_parallel_queries_over_time}. We observe two complementary querying strategies. The first is \emph{multi-query} search, where multiple Web queries are issued in parallel within the same stage. The second is \emph{iterative} search, where subsequent Web queries are generated after examining earlier search results. ChatGPT, Grok, and DeepSeek employ both strategies. In contrast, Claude relies predominantly on iterative search, issuing fewer parallel queries but performing more refinement. These observations indicate that conversational agents orchestrate complex querying strategies before generating responses.

